    {
      "n": 2,
      "title": "Glycolysis",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIa-j-7, -8",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Describe the overall process of cellular respiration.</li><li>Explain the steps of glycolysis.</li><li>Identify the products of glycolysis.</li><li>Explain substrate-level phosphorylation.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Glycolysis</strong> — breakdown of glucose into 2 pyruvate.</li><li><strong>Substrate-level phosphorylation</strong> — direct ATP production.</li><li><strong>Net ATP</strong> — 2 ATP per glucose (4 produced − 2 used).</li><li><strong>NADH</strong> — carries electrons to the ETC.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Glycolysis Overview</h4><p>Occurs in cytoplasm. Glucose (6C) is split into 2 pyruvate (3C) molecules.</p><h4>B. Two Phases</h4><ul><li><strong>Investment phase</strong> — 2 ATP used to activate glucose</li><li><strong>Payoff phase</strong> — 4 ATP and 2 NADH produced</li></ul><h4>C. Net Products (per glucose)</h4><ul><li>2 ATP (net)</li><li>2 NADH</li><li>2 pyruvate</li></ul>",
      "activity1": {
        "timeLimit": 90,
        "badgeId": "glycolysis-master",
        "badgeName": "Glycolysis Master",
        "badgeIcon": "🧪",
        "pairs": [
          { "key": "gly", "left": "Glycolysis", "right": "Glucose → 2 pyruvate" },
          { "key": "loc", "left": "Location", "right": "Cytoplasm" },
          { "key": "inv", "left": "Investment phase", "right": "Uses 2 ATP" },
          { "key": "pay", "left": "Payoff phase", "right": "Produces 4 ATP" },
          { "key": "net", "left": "Net ATP", "right": "2 per glucose" },
          { "key": "nadh", "left": "NADH", "right": "Carries electrons to ETC" }
        ]
      },
      "activity2": {
        "timePerCard": 12,
        "badgeId": "glyco-detective",
